GEEKSFORGEEKS:Largest subarray with 0 sum
Given an array arr[] containing both positive and negative integers, the task is to find the length 
of the longest subarray with a sum equals to 0.

Note: A subarray is a contiguous part of an array, formed by selecting one or more 
consecutive elements while maintaining their original order.

Examples:
Input: arr[] = [15, -2, 2, -8, 1, 7, 10, 23]
Output: 5
Explanation: The longest subarray with sum equals to 0 is [-2, 2, -8, 1, 7].
Input: arr[] = [2, 10, 4]
Output: 0
Explanation: There is no subarray with a sum of 0.
Input: arr[] = [1, 0, -4, 3, 1, 0]
Output: 5
Explanation: The longest subarray with sum equals to 0 is [0, -4, 3, 1, 0]
Constraints:
1 ≤ arr.size() ≤ 106
−103 ≤ arr[i] ≤ 103
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
🧠 Interview Recall Bullets
• Find longest zero-sum subarray
• Use prefix equality form
• Map stores first prefix position
• When prefix repeats → update max length
• O(N) optimal solution
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
OPTIMAL SOLUTION: TIME COMPLEXITY : O(N) || SPACE COMPLEXITY : O(N) :

class Solution {
    int maxLength(int arr[]) {
         int prefixsum=0,result=0;
        Map<Integer,Integer> mapp=new HashMap<>();
        mapp.put(0,0);
        for(int i=0;i<arr.length;i++)
        {
            prefixsum=prefixsum+arr[i];
            if(mapp.containsKey(prefixsum))
            {
                int temp=mapp.get(prefixsum);
                result=Math.max(result,(i+1-temp));
            }
            else
            {
                mapp.put(prefixsum,i+1);
            }
        }
        return result;
    }
}
